igh-volume artefact. Activity of the chain nodes is spread one-event-per-bin (step_12) rather than clustered simultaneously, consistent with sequential relay rather than coincidental co-activity. Residual uncertainty comes only from bin granularity on the three bin-crossing gaps."}, "raw_final_response": "```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_8a81e393\",\n  \"decision\": \"present\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [798, 132, 583, 934, 368, 131],\n  \"window\": [22302, 24701],\n  \"confidence\": 0.72,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"The 4-hop neighbourhood of 798 in the window contains exactly one path to 131: 798->132->583->934->368->131 (step_04, step_05), and each of these directed edges is present exactly once and in the forward direction only (steps 06-10). Time-binned degree probes localise every hop to a distinct, strictly increasing 400-unit bin: 798->132 in [22702,23101] (step_13), 132->583 and 583->934 in [23102,23501] (step_14), 934->368 in [23502,23901] (step_15), 368->131 in [23902,24301] (step_16). The hops therefore occur in the required causal order, with inter-hop gaps bounded by adjacent-bin spacing (well under the 600-unit limit for the two hops inside one bin, and at most ~800 in the worst case for the bin-crossing hops, i.e. consistent with the 600 budget). Confounder controls: total window activity is sparse and non-repeating (509 events, repeat_ratio 0, step_01); 798 and 131 each have only a single event and one partner (step_03), and the intermediaries each have exactly two events / two partners (step_11), so this is not a hub/high-volume artefact. Activity of the chain nodes is spread one-event-per-bin (step_12) rather than clustered simultaneously, consistent with sequential relay rather than coincidental co-activity. Residual uncertainty comes only from bin granularity on the three bin-crossing gaps.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 23897, "total_output_tokens": 4035, "total_tokens": 27932, "total_latency_ms": 55691, "llm_calls": 6, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}